From 7bd2366fa536c950b3574431c77ad5df4f89aefd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReykoMe <ReykoMe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kms: render evdi/DisplayLink outputs on the primary GPU

evdi devices have no render engine, so their EGL display is backed by
llvmpipe. Outputs on such devices were either composited entirely with
llvmpipe or rendered on the primary GPU and then copied back through the
CPU ("Falling back to cpu-copy"), because importing the primary GPU's
tiled/CCS buffers into the evdi device fails. On a 3440x1440@100 Hz
DisplayLink monitor this costs several CPU cores while windows move.

After initialize_output(), replace the swapchain allocator of software
targets with a GBM allocator on the primary GPU using the linear
modifier, and render those outputs with a single renderer on the primary
GPU. The framebuffer exporter imports the linear dmabuf into evdi, so
no llvmpipe composition or CPU copy is involved.

Based on the approach proposed in pop-os/cosmic-comp#2109.
---
